---This resource represents a long-running operation that is the result of a network API call.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.Operation
---@field done? boolean If the value is `false`, it means the operation is still in progress. If `true`, the operation is completed, and either `error` or `response` is available.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.DocumentMap Service-specific metadata associated with the operation. It typically contains progress information and common metadata such as create time. Some services might not provide such metadata. Any method that returns a long-running operation should document the metadata type, if any.
---@field response? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.DocumentMap The normal, successful response of the operation. If the original method returns no data on success, such as `Delete`, the response is `google.protobuf.Empty`. If the original method is standard `Get`/`Create`/`Update`, the response should be the resource. For other methods, the response should have the type `XxxResponse`, where `Xxx` is the original method name. For example, if the original method name is `TakeSnapshot()`, the inferred response type is `TakeSnapshotResponse`.
---@field error? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.Status The error result of the operation in case of failure or cancellation.
---@field name? string The server-assigned name, which is only unique within the same service that originally returns it. If you use the default HTTP mapping, the `name` should be a resource name ending with `operations/{unique_id}`.

---This represents a particular package that is distributed over various channels. e.g. glibc (aka libc6) is distributed by many, at various versions.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.Package
---@field packageType? string The type of package; whether native or non native (e.g., ruby gems, node.js packages, etc.).
---@field cpeUri? string The cpe_uri in [CPE format](https://cpe.mitre.org/specification/) denoting the package manager version distributing a package. The cpe_uri will be blank for language packages.
---@field description? string The description of this package.
---@field url? string The homepage for this package.
---@field version? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.Version The version of the package.
---@field architecture? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.PackageArchitectureEnum|string The CPU architecture for which packages in this distribution channel were built. Architecture will be blank for language packages.
---@field distribution? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.DistributionList The various channels by which a package is distributed.
---@field digest? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.DigestList Hash value, typically a file digest, that allows unique identification a specific package.
---@field name? string The name of the package.
---@field maintainer? string A freeform text denoting the maintainer of this package.
---@field license? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.License Licenses that have been declared by the authors of the package.

---@alias gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.PackageArchitectureEnum "ARCHITECTURE_UNSPECIFIED"|"X86"|"X64"

---PackageInfoNote represents an SPDX Package Information section: https://spdx.github.io/spdx-spec/3-package-information/
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.PackageInfoNote
---@field filesLicenseInfo? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.StringList Contain the license the SPDX file creator has concluded as governing the This field is to contain a list of all licenses found in the package. The relationship between licenses (i.e., conjunctive, disjunctive) is not specified in this field – it is simply a listing of all licenses found
---@field summaryDescription? string A short description of the package
---@field analyzed? boolean Indicates whether the file content of this package has been available for or subjected to analysis when creating the SPDX document
---@field externalRefs? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.ExternalRefList ExternalRef
---@field packageType? string The type of package: OS, MAVEN, GO, GO_STDLIB, etc.
---@field detailedDescription? string A more detailed description of the package
---@field checksum? string Provide an independently reproducible mechanism that permits unique identification of a specific package that correlates to the data in this SPDX file
---@field version? string Identify the version of the package
---@field attribution? string A place for the SPDX data creator to record, at the package level, acknowledgements that may be needed to be communicated in some contexts
---@field copyright? string Identify the copyright holders of the package, as well as any dates present
---@field downloadLocation? string This section identifies the download Universal Resource Locator (URL), or a specific location within a version control system (VCS) for the package at the time that the SPDX file was created
---@field originator? string If the package identified in the SPDX file originated from a different person or organization than identified as Package Supplier, this field identifies from where or whom the package originally came
---@field homePage? string Provide a place for the SPDX file creator to record a web site that serves as the package's home page
---@field licenseDeclared? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.License List the licenses that have been declared by the authors of the package
---@field title? string Identify the full name of the package as given by the Package Originator
---@field verificationCode? string This field provides an independently reproducible mechanism identifying specific contents of a package based on the actual files (except the SPDX file itself, if it is included in the package) that make up each package and that correlates to the data in this SPDX file
---@field supplier? string Identify the actual distribution source for the package/directory identified in the SPDX file

---PackageInfoOccurrence represents an SPDX Package Information section: https://spdx.github.io/spdx-spec/3-package-information/
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.PackageInfoOccurrence
---@field summaryDescription? string Output only. A short description of the package
---@field title? string Output only. Identify the full name of the package as given by the Package Originator
---@field comment? string A place for the SPDX file creator to record any general comments about the package being described
---@field homePage? string Output only. Provide a place for the SPDX file creator to record a web site that serves as the package's home page
---@field packageType? string Output only. The type of package: OS, MAVEN, GO, GO_STDLIB, etc.
---@field filename? string Provide the actual file name of the package, or path of the directory being treated as a package
---@field version? string Output only. Identify the version of the package
---@field licenseConcluded? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.License package or alternative values, if the governing license cannot be determined
---@field sourceInfo? string Provide a place for the SPDX file creator to record any relevant background information or additional comments about the origin of the package
---@field id? string Uniquely identify any element in an SPDX document which may be referenced by other elements

