---@field buildType? string URI indicating what type of build was performed.
---@field builder? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.GoogleDevtoolsContaineranalysisV1alpha1SlsaProvenanceZeroTwoSlsaBuilder Identifies the entity that executed the recipe, which is trusted to have correctly performed the operation and populated this provenance.
---@field materials? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.GoogleDevtoolsContaineranalysisV1alpha1SlsaProvenanceZeroTwoSlsaMaterialList The collection of artifacts that influenced the build including sources, dependencies, build tools, base images, and so on.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.GoogleDevtoolsContaineranalysisV1alpha1SlsaProvenanceZeroTwoSlsaMetadata Other properties of the build.
---@field invocation? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.GoogleDevtoolsContaineranalysisV1alpha1SlsaProvenanceZeroTwoSlsaInvocation Identifies the event that kicked off the build.
---@field buildConfig? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.DocumentMap Lists the steps in the build.

---Steps taken to build the artifact. For a TaskRun, typically each container corresponds to one step in the recipe.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.SlsaRecipe
---@field type? string URI indicating what type of recipe was performed. It determines the meaning of recipe.entryPoint, recipe.arguments, recipe.environment, and materials.
---@field entryPoint? string String identifying the entry point into the build. This is often a path to a configuration file and/or a target label within that file. The syntax and meaning are defined by recipe.type. For example, if the recipe type were "make", then this would reference the directory in which to run make as well as which target to use.
---@field arguments? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.DocumentMap Collection of all external inputs that influenced the build on top of recipe.definedInMaterial and recipe.entryPoint. For example, if the recipe type were "make", then this might be the flags passed to make aside from the target, which is captured in recipe.entryPoint. Depending on the recipe Type, the structure may be different.
---@field definedInMaterial? string Index in materials containing the recipe steps that are not implied by recipe.type. For example, if the recipe type were "make", then this would point to the source containing the Makefile, not the make program itself. Set to -1 if the recipe doesn't come from a material, as zero is default unset value for int64.
---@field environment? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.DocumentMap Any other builder-controlled inputs necessary for correctly evaluating the recipe. Usually only needed for reproducing the build but not evaluated as part of policy. Depending on the recipe Type, the structure may be different.

---Source describes the location of the source used for the build.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.Source
---@field repoSource? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.RepoSource If provided, get source from this location in a Cloud Repo.
---@field storageSource? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.StorageSource If provided, get the source from this location in Google Cloud Storage.
---@field artifactStorageSource? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.StorageSource If provided, the input binary artifacts for the build came from this location.
---@field context? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.GoogleDevtoolsContaineranalysisV1alpha1SourceContext If provided, the source code used for the build came from this location.
---@field fileHashes? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.FileHashesMap Hash(es) of the build source, which can be used to verify that the original source integrity was maintained in the build. The keys to this map are file paths used as build source and the values contain the hash values for those files. If the build source came in a single package such as a gzipped tarfile (.tar.gz), the FileHash will be for the single path to that file.
---@field additionalContexts? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.GoogleDevtoolsContaineranalysisV1alpha1SourceContextList If provided, some of the source code used for the build may be found in these locations, in the case where the source repository had multiple remotes or submodules. This list will not include the context specified in the context field.

---The `Status` type defines a logical error model that is suitable for different programming environments, including REST APIs and RPC APIs. It is used by [gRPC](https://github.com/grpc). Each `Status` message contains three pieces of data: error code, error message, and error details. You can find out more about this error model and how to work with it in the [API Design Guide](https://cloud.google.com/apis/design/errors).
