---The Upgrade Distribution represents metadata about the Upgrade for each operating system (CPE). Some distributions have additional metadata around updates, classifying them into various categories and severities.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.UpgradeDistribution
---@field severity? string The severity as specified by the upstream operating system.
---@field cpeUri? string Required - The specific operating system this metadata applies to. See https://cpe.mitre.org/specification/.
---@field classification? string The operating system classification of this Upgrade, as specified by the upstream operating system upgrade feed.
---@field cve? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.StringList The cve that would be resolved by this upgrade.

---@alias gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.UpgradeDistributionList gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.UpgradeDistribution[]

---An Upgrade Note represents a potential upgrade of a package to a given version. For each package version combination (i.e. bash 4.0, bash 4.1, bash 4.1.2), there will be a Upgrade Note.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.UpgradeNote
---@field version? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.Version Required - The version of the package in machine + human readable form.
---@field package? string Required - The package this Upgrade is for.
---@field distributions? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.UpgradeDistributionList Metadata about the upgrade for each specific operating system.

---An Upgrade Occurrence represents that a specific resource_url could install a specific upgrade. This presence is supplied via local sources (i.e. it is present in the mirror and the running system has noticed its availability).
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.UpgradeOccurrence
---@field package? string Required - The package this Upgrade is for.
---@field parsedVersion? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.Version Required - The version of the package in a machine + human readable form.
---@field distribution? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.UpgradeDistribution Metadata about the upgrade for available for the specific operating system for the resource_url. This allows efficient filtering, as well as making it easier to use the occurrence.

---Version contains structured information about the version of the package. For a discussion of this in Debian/Ubuntu: http://serverfault.com/questions/604541/debian-packages-version-convention For a discussion of this in Redhat/Fedora/Centos: http://blog.jasonantman.com/2014/07/how-yum-and-rpm-compare-versions/
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.Version
---@field name? string The main part of the version name.
---@field kind? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VersionKindEnum|string Distinguish between sentinel MIN/MAX versions and normal versions. If kind is not NORMAL, then the other fields are ignored.
---@field revision? string The iteration of the package build from the above version.
---@field epoch? number Used to correct mistakes in the version numbering scheme.
---@field inclusive? boolean Whether this version is vulnerable, when defining the version bounds. For example, if the minimum version is 2.0, inclusive=true would say 2.0 is vulnerable, while inclusive=false would say it's not

---@alias gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VersionKindEnum "NORMAL"|"MINIMUM"|"MAXIMUM"

---VexAssessment provides all publisher provided Vex information that is related to this vulnerability.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VexAssessment
---@field justification? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.Justification Justification provides the justification when the state of the assessment if NOT_AFFECTED.
---@field vulnerabilityId? string The vulnerability identifier for this Assessment. Will hold one of common identifiers e.g. CVE, GHSA etc.
---@field remediations? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.RemediationList Specifies details on how to handle (and presumably, fix) a vulnerability.
---@field relatedUris? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.URIList Holds a list of references associated with this vulnerability item and assessment. These uris have additional information about the vulnerability and the assessment itself. E.g. Link to a document which details how this assessment concluded the state of this vulnerability.
---@field cve? string Holds the MITRE standard Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures (CVE) tracking number for the vulnerability.
---@field impacts? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.StringList Contains information about the impact of this vulnerability, this will change with time.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VexAssessmentStateEnum|string Provides the state of this Vulnerability assessment.
---@field noteName? string The VulnerabilityAssessment note from which this VexAssessment was generated. This will be of the form: `projects/[PROJECT_ID]/notes/[NOTE_ID]`.

---@alias gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VexAssessmentStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"AFFECTED"|"NOT_AFFECTED"|"FIXED"|"UNDER_INVESTIGATION"

---A single VulnerabilityAssessmentNote represents one particular product's vulnerability assessment for one CVE. Multiple VulnerabilityAssessmentNotes together form a Vex statement. Please go/sds-vex-example for a sample Vex statement in the CSAF format.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VulnerabilityAssessmentNote
---@field languageCode? string Identifies the language used by this document, corresponding to IETF BCP 47 / RFC 5646.
---@field assessment? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.Assessment Represents a vulnerability assessment for the product.
---@field title? string The title of the note. E.g. `Vex-Debian-11.4`
---@field publisher? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.Publisher Publisher details of this Note.
---@field product? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.Product The product affected by this vex.
---@field longDescription? string A detailed description of this Vex.
---@field shortDescription? string A one sentence description of this Vex.

---The status of a vulnerability attestation generation.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VulnerabilityAttestation
---@field state? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VulnerabilityAttestationStateEnum|string Output only. The success/failure state of the latest attestation attempt.
---@field error? string Output only. If failure, the error reason for why the attestation generation failed.
---@field lastAttemptTime? string Output only. The last time we attempted to generate an attestation.

---@alias gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VulnerabilityAttestationStateEnum "VULNERABILITY_ATTESTATION_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SUCCESS"|"FAILURE"

---Used by Occurrence to point to where the vulnerability exists and how to fix it.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VulnerabilityDetails
---@field vexAssessment? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VexAssessment VexAssessment provides all publisher provided Vex information that is related to this vulnerability for this resource.
---@field cvssV4? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.CVSS Optional. The CVSS v4 score of this vulnerability.
---@field effectiveSeverity? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VulnerabilityDetailsEffectiveSeverityEnum|string The distro assigned severity for this vulnerability when that is available and note provider assigned severity when distro has not yet assigned a severity for this vulnerability. When there are multiple package issues for this vulnerability, they can have different effective severities because some might come from the distro and some might come from installed language packs (e.g. Maven JARs or Go binaries). For this reason, it is advised to use the effective severity on the PackageIssue level, as this field may eventually be deprecated. In the case where multiple PackageIssues have different effective severities, the one set here will be the highest severity of any of the PackageIssues.
---@field type? string The type of package; whether native or non native(ruby gems, node.js packages etc). This may be deprecated in the future because we can have multiple PackageIssues with different package types.
---@field cvssVersion? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VulnerabilityDetailsCvssVersionEnum|string Output only. CVSS version used to populate cvss_score and severity.
---@field cvssV2? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.CVSS The CVSS v2 score of this vulnerability.
---@field extraDetails? string Occurrence-specific extra details about the vulnerability.
---@field severity? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VulnerabilityDetailsSeverityEnum|string Output only. The note provider assigned Severity of the vulnerability.
---@field cvssScore? number Output only. The CVSS score of this vulnerability. CVSS score is on a scale of 0-10 where 0 indicates low severity and 10 indicates high severity.
---@field cvssV3? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.CVSS The CVSS v3 score of this vulnerability.
---@field risk? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.Risk Risk information about the vulnerability, such as CISA, EPSS, etc.
---@field packageIssue? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.PackageIssueList The set of affected locations and their fixes (if available) within the associated resource.

---@alias gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VulnerabilityDetailsCvssVersionEnum "CVSS_VERSION_UNSPECIFIED"|"CVSS_VERSION_2"|"CVSS_VERSION_3"|"CVSS_VERSION_4"

---@alias gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VulnerabilityDetailsEffectiveSeverityEnum "SEVERITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"MINIMAL"|"LOW"|"MEDIUM"|"HIGH"|"CRITICAL"

---@alias gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VulnerabilityDetailsSeverityEnum "SEVERITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"MINIMAL"|"LOW"|"MEDIUM"|"HIGH"|"CRITICAL"

---The location of the vulnerability
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VulnerabilityLocation
---@field package? string The package being described.
---@field cpeUri? string The cpe_uri in [cpe format] (https://cpe.mitre.org/specification/) format. Examples include distro or storage location for vulnerable jar. This field can be used as a filter in list requests.
---@field fileLocation? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.FileLocationList The file location at which this package was found.
---@field version? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.Version The version of the package being described. This field can be used as a filter in list requests.

---VulnerabilityType provides metadata about a security vulnerability.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VulnerabilityType
---@field cvssVersion? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VulnerabilityTypeCvssVersionEnum|string CVSS version used to populate cvss_score and severity.
---@field cvssV2? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.CVSS The full description of the CVSS for version 2.
---@field cvssScore? number The CVSS score for this Vulnerability.
---@field details? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.DetailList All information about the package to specifically identify this vulnerability. One entry per (version range and cpe_uri) the package vulnerability has manifested in.
---@field severity? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VulnerabilityTypeSeverityEnum|string Note provider assigned impact of the vulnerability
---@field cwe? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.StringList A list of CWE for this vulnerability. For details, see: https://cwe.mitre.org/index.html
---@field advisoryPublishTime? string Time this advisory was published by the source.
---@field cvssV4? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.CVSS Optional. The full description of the CVSS for version 4.

---@alias gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VulnerabilityTypeCvssVersionEnum "CVSS_VERSION_UNSPECIFIED"|"CVSS_VERSION_2"|"CVSS_VERSION_3"|"CVSS_VERSION_4"

---@alias gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1alpha1.VulnerabilityTypeSeverityEnum "SEVERITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"MINIMAL"|"LOW"|"MEDIUM"|"HIGH"|"CRITICAL"

---Result of Workspace Policy scan.
